PART 8 – FIVE-OPTION MCQ & SPECIAL ANSWER SYSTEM

ALL questions in both Common GS and Language papers must have exactly FIVE options.

Display:

A
B
C
D
E – DON'T KNOW / पता नहीं

Option E is a special response.

When the aspirant does not know the answer, they can select Option E.

Also provide a separate NOT ATTEMPTED state.

IMPORTANT DIFFERENCE:

1. Option E means the aspirant has consciously selected "I Don't Know".
2. NOT ATTEMPTED means the aspirant has not selected any option and leaves the question unanswered.

These two states must be stored separately.

ANSWER SCORING RULES

Apply the following scoring system to both the 40-question Common GS paper and the 30-question Language paper.

Answer Status| Marks
Correct Answer| +1
Incorrect Answer| -1/3
Option E – Don't Know| 0
Completely Unselected / Not Attempted| -1/3

IMPORTANT:

- Every three incorrect answers result in a deduction of one mark.
- Three completely unselected questions also result in a deduction of one mark.
- Selecting Option E results in zero marks and no negative marking.
- Option E must not be counted as an unanswered question.
- Completely unselected questions must be counted separately.
- Do not combine incorrect answers and Option E responses.
- Show the number of correct, incorrect, Don't Know and Not Attempted responses separately.

The total score must be calculated accurately, including fractional marks.

Do not silently round intermediate calculations.

Display scores up to two decimal places.

At final submission, every question must be assigned one of these four statuses.

Provide an Admin-configurable scoring policy, but preserve the above default rules.

